+schemaVersion: 1
+
+feature: team-spaces
+language: typescript
+context: Audit
+
+intent: >-
+  `GET /audit/spaces/:id` answers a space's admins its activity, most recent first, as [{ at,
+  actorId, action, subject }]: member-invited, member-joined, member-removed, member-left,
+  role-changed (subject: the account), note-written, note-edited, note-archived, note-restored
+  (subject: the note); anyone else gets 403. Audit is fed only by the facts of
+  SpaceIntegrationEvents.ts (Teams) and NoteChangedIntegrationEvent (Notes), both frozen; it learns
+  the admins from them. Fill the module and the routes under `/audit`. The other slices are written
+  at the same time.
+
+changes:
+  - kind: integration-event
+    name: MemberInvitedIntegrationEvent
+    aggregate: Space
+    new: false
+  - kind: aggregate
+    name: Activity
+    new: true
+  - kind: query
+    name: GetSpaceActivity
+    verb: read
+    route: GET /audit/spaces/:id
+    new: true
+
+invariants:
+  - Audit reads no other context's store and imports no other context's Domain.
+  - A note's change is recorded only for a space's note; the actor of a membership fact is who did it (joining and leaving are the member's own).
+
+events:
+  - ActivityRecordedEvent
+
+crossContext:
+  context: Teams
+  strategy: integration-event
+  why: >-
+    A space's activity is what Teams publishes about its members (and what Notes publishes about its
+    notes, the same way).
+
+architectureChanges: false
