+schemaVersion: 1
+
+feature: team-spaces
+language: typescript
+context: Notes
+
+intent: >-
+  A note may belong to a space (`spaceId`): an editor or an admin writes one, edits, archives and
+  restores any of the space's notes; any member lists them (`GET /notes?space=`) and reads them; a
+  reader changes nothing; pinning, tagging, sharing and reminders are refused on a space's note; "my
+  notes" lists personal notes only. A space's notes count against the space's limit (Plans' frozen
+  `spacePlanReadModel`), never a personal quota. Notes asks the role through a port it owns
+  (SpaceMembership), answered over Teams' frozen `spaceQueries` (ISpaceQueries). Publish
+  NoteChangedIntegrationEvent (frozen in NoteIntegrationEvents.ts) through the outbox on every
+  change: written, edited, archived, restored, shared. The other slices are written at the same time.
+
+changes:
+  - kind: aggregate
+    name: Note
+    new: false
+  - kind: domain-service
+    name: SpaceNoteAccess
+    aggregate: Note
+    new: true
+  - kind: integration-event
+    name: NoteChangedIntegrationEvent
+    aggregate: Note
+    new: false
+
+invariants:
+  - What a role may do to a space's note is decided in Notes' Domain or Application layer, from the port; nothing in Notes' Domain imports Teams.
+  - A member removed from a space reads none of its notes from then on (404).
+  - Each note in a read answers `spaceId`, null for a personal note.
+
+events:
+  - NoteCreatedEvent
+
+crossContext:
+  context: Teams
+  strategy: owned-port
+  why: >-
+    What a member may do to a space's note depends on their role, which only Teams knows. (Notes
+    also asks Plans a space's note limit over its read model, and publishes NoteChanged to Search
+    and Audit.)
+
+architectureChanges: false
