+schemaVersion: 1
+
+feature: team-spaces
+language: typescript
+context: Plans
+
+intent: >-
+  A space is on Free (3 seats, 50 notes) until one of its admins switches it to Team with a number
+  of seats (no note limit); `GET /plans/spaces/:id` answers members only, exactly { plan, seats,
+  noteLimit }. Plans learns a space's admins and members from what Teams publishes
+  (SpaceIntegrationEvents.ts, frozen), and refuses a plan with fewer seats than members. Replace the
+  stub `spacePlanReadModel` (the frozen ISpacePlanQueries) with one answering from your store:
+  Teams and Notes read it. The other slices are written at the same time.
+
+changes:
+  - kind: integration-event
+    name: SpaceCreatedIntegrationEvent
+    aggregate: Space
+    new: false
+  - kind: integration-event
+    name: MemberJoinedIntegrationEvent
+    aggregate: Space
+    new: false
+  - kind: aggregate
+    name: SpacePlan
+    new: true
+  - kind: command
+    name: ChangeSpacePlan
+    verb: replace
+    route: PUT /plans/spaces/:id
+    new: true
+  - kind: query
+    name: GetSpacePlan
+    verb: read
+    route: GET /plans/spaces/:id
+    new: true
+
+invariants:
+  - Only an admin of the space changes its plan; Team needs a number of seats, never fewer than the space's members; Free is 3 seats.
+  - A space that never chose is on Free without anything having created a plan for it.
+  - A non-member reading a space's plan gets 404.
+
+events:
+  - SpacePlanChangedEvent
+
+crossContext:
+  context: Teams
+  strategy: integration-event
+  why: >-
+    Plans needs a space's admins and members; Teams publishes who joins, leaves, is removed and
+    changes role.
+
+architectureChanges: false
